sweet usb: sending works again after a long unplug (0223).

all-16 with 0220 (2026-11-18): a re-enumeration after a short interruption (392 s) carried on normally. After an hour without
the cable the Mac's en3 came up "active" (0220's part) but got no frame back: ue0 rx went on counting (415 -> 579), tx stayed
at 3599. While unplugged the send queue had filled (live log); ud_if_output drops when the queue is full and returns before
the kick, and the transfer whose completion would have kicked had been ended by the bus reset. Now the bus-reset teardown
frees the queued frames (they are stale), and ud_if_output kicks before it looks at the queue.
Not run on hardware yet.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index 6b82ce8..b3cf0f9 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -475,6 +475,17 @@ ud_deconfigure(const char *why)
 	lck_mtx_lock(ud.lock);
 	ud.configured = false;
 	ud.tx_busy = false;
+	/*
+	 * 0223: drop what queued up while the cable was out. all-16: after an hour unplugged the queue held
+	 * UD_TXQ frames; ud_if_output drops (and does not kick) when the queue is full, the transfer whose
+	 * completion would have kicked was ended above, so after the new enumeration ue0 received (rx 415 ->
+	 * 579) but never sent again (tx stayed 3599).
+	 */
+	while (ud.txq_count > 0) {
+		mbuf_freem(ud.txq[ud.txq_head]);
+		ud.txq_head = (ud.txq_head + 1) % UD_TXQ;
+		ud.txq_count--;
+	}
 	lck_mtx_unlock(ud.lock);
 	ud.data_alt = 0;
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
@@ -679,6 +690,7 @@ static errno_t
 ud_if_output(ifnet_t ifp, mbuf_t m)
 {
 	lck_mtx_lock(ud.lock);
+	ud_tx_kick_locked();            /* 0223: a full queue with an idle endpoint must not stay that way */
 	if (ud.txq_count == UD_TXQ || !ud.configured) {
 		lck_mtx_unlock(ud.lock);
 		mbuf_freem(m);
